<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The floating warning card's own copy. Kept apart from strings.xml so the overlay redesign merges
  cleanly alongside the child and parent app work.

  Same reader as the overlay strings in strings.xml: a teenager, mid-message. Every line here is
  written to be read in a second, to explain rather than accuse, and to never imply that anyone
  is watching or that they are in trouble. "Why it matters" beats "what you did wrong".
-->
<resources>
    <!--
      The supporting line under the card's title: why this kind of thing is worth a second
      thought. One per category, because a single generic "this could be risky" line is exactly
      the kind of message people learn to tap past. The title already says *what* was spotted.
    -->
    <string name="overlay_why_pii">Once it\'s sent, you can\'t control who else sees it.</string>
    <string name="overlay_why_harassment">Words like these can land harder than you meant.</string>
    <string name="overlay_why_solicitation">You never have to send anything you\'re not comfortable with.</string>
    <string name="overlay_why_self_harm">If things feel heavy, you don\'t have to handle them alone.</string>
    <string name="overlay_why_violence">Even as a joke, this can read as a real threat.</string>
    <string name="overlay_why_meetup">Meeting someone new? Let an adult you trust know the plan.</string>
    <string name="overlay_why_substance">Messages like this can be screenshotted and shared.</string>

    <!--
      The paused notice when Ignore is on offer too. The plain overlay_typing_paused is only true
      when removing is the one way out; telling someone who can tap Ignore that removing is
      their only option would be a small lie told at exactly the wrong moment.
    -->
    <string name="overlay_typing_paused_or_ignore">Typing is paused until you remove this or tap Ignore.</string>

    <!--
      The crisis supporting line when the region has no named helpline. The fallback resource's
      label is an instruction ("Find a helpline near you") rather than a name, so it cannot be
      slotted into overlay_crisis_detail: the old copy came out as "Find a helpline near you can
      help, and it's free."
    -->
    <string name="overlay_crisis_support_generic">You don\'t have to go through this alone. Talking to someone can really help, and it\'s free.</string>

    <!-- Spoken by TalkBack for the leading icon, so the severity is never carried by colour alone. -->
    <string name="overlay_icon_high">Important</string>
    <string name="overlay_icon_medium">Heads up</string>
    <string name="overlay_icon_crisis">Support</string>
    <!-- Announced when the card appears, like a window title. -->
    <string name="overlay_pane_title">Keyguard</string>
</resources>
